{
  "title": "50: Qaaf ق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nقٓۚ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ الْمَجِيْدِۚ‏(1)\nQAA WAL QURAANIL AL-MAJEEDE.\nQaf: By the Glorious Qur'an (Thou art Allah's Messenger). \nبَلْ عَجِبُوْۤا اَنْ جَآءَهُمْ مُّنْذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَقَالَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا شَىْءٌ عَجِيْبٌ‌ۚ‏(2)\nBAL A’AJEBOOA AN JAAA-AHUM MMUNZERUN MINHUM FAQAALA KAAFEROON HAAZAA SHAY-UN A’AJEEBUN.\nBut they wonder that there has come to them a Warner from among themselves. So the Unbelievers say: “This is a wonderful thing! \nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا ‌ۚ ذٰ لِكَ رَجْعٌ ۢ بَعِيْدٌ‏(3)\nA-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW ZAA LEKA RAJA’UN BAE’EEDUN.\n“What! When we die and become dust, (shall we live again?) That is a (sort of) return far (from our understanding).” \nقَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنْقُصُ الْاَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَعِنْدَنَا كِتٰبٌ حَفِيْظٌ‏(4)\nQAD A’LIMNAA MAA TANQUSU ARZO MINHUM WAE’ENDANAA KETAABUM HAFEEZUN.\nWe already know how much of them the earth takes away: With Us is a record guarding (the full account). \nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ فَهُمْ فِىْۤ اَمْرٍ مَّرِيْجٍ‏(5)\nBAL KAZZABOO BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM FAHUM FEE AMRIN MMAREEJIN.\nBut they deny the Truth when it comes to them: so they are in a confused state. \nاَ فَلَمْ يَنْظُرُوْۤا اِلَى السَّمَآءِ فَوْقَهُمْ كَيْفَ بَنَيْنٰهَا وَزَ يَّنّٰهَا وَمَا لَهَا مِنْ فُرُوْجٍ‏(6)\nA-FALAM YANZUROOA ELAL SAMAAA-E FAWQAHUM KAYFA BANAYNAAHAA WAZA YYANNAAHAA WA MAA LAHAA MIN FUROOJIN.\nDo they not look at the sky above them? How We have made it and adorned it, and there are no flaws in it? \nوَالْاَرْضَ مَدَدْنٰهَا وَاَ لْقَيْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍۢ بَهِيْجٍ ۙ‏(7)\nWAL ARZA MADADNAAHAA WAALQAYNAA FEEHAA JA-A’LA WAANBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIN BAHEEJIN.\nAnd the earth- We have spread it out, and set thereon mountains standing firm, and produced therein every kind of beautiful growth (in pairs)- \nتَبْصِرَةً وَّذِكْرٰى لِكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيْبٍ‏(8)\nTABSERATAN WA ZIKRAA LEKULLIM A’ABDIN MMUNEEBIN.\nTo be observed and commemorated by every devotee turning (to Allah). \nوَنَزَّلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً مُّبٰرَكًا فَاَنْۢبَتْنَا بِهٖ جَنّٰتٍ وَّحَبَّ الْحَصِيْدِ ۙ‏(9)\nWA NAZZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN MMUBAARAKAN FA-ANBATNAA BEHI JANNAATIN WWAHABBA AL-HASEEDE.\nAnd We send down from the sky rain charted with blessing, and We produce therewith gardens and Grain for harvests; \nوَالنَّخْلَ بٰسِقٰتٍ لَّهَا طَلْعٌ نَّضِيْدٌ ۙ‏(10)\nWAALNNAKHLA BAASEQAATIN LLAHAA TALA’UN NNAZEEDUN.\nAnd tall (and stately) palm-trees, with shoots of fruit-stalks, piled one over another;- \nرِّزْقًا لِّلْعِبَادِ‌ ۙ وَاَحْيَيْنَا بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا‌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ الْخُرُوْجُ‏(11)\nRIZQAN LLELE’EBAADE WAAHYAYNAA BEHI BALDATAN MMAYTAN KAZAALEKA AL-KHUROOJU.\nAs sustenance for (Allah's) Servants;- and We give (new) life therewith to land that is dead: Thus will be the Resurrection. \nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّاَصْحٰبُ الرَّسِّ وَثَمُوْدُۙ‏(12)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WWAASHAABU AR-RASSE WA SAMOODO.\nBefore them was denied (the Hereafter) by the People of Noah, the Companions of the Rass, the Thamud, \nوَعَادٌ وَّفِرْعَوْنُ وَاِخْوَانُ لُوْطٍۙ‏(13)\nWA A’ADUN WWAFERA’AWNU WAAKHWAANU LOOTIM.\nThe 'Ad, Pharaoh, the brethren of Lut, \nوَّاَصْحٰبُ الْاَيْكَةِ وَقَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ‌ؕ كُلٌّ كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيْدِ‏(14)\nWWAASHAABU AL-AAYKATE WA QAWMO TUBBAA’IN KULLUL KAZZABA AR-RUSULA FA HAQQA WAE’EEDE.\nThe Companions of the Wood, and the People of Tubba'; each one (of them) rejected the messengers, and My warning was duly fulfilled (in them). \nاَفَعَيِيْنَا بِالْخَلْقِ الْاَوَّلِ‌ؕ بَلْ هُمْ فِىْ لَبْسٍ مِّنْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ‏(15)\nAAFAA’AYEENAA BIL-KHALQE AL-AAWLE BAL HUM FEE LABSIN MIN KHALQIN JADEEDIN.\nWere We then weary with the first Creation, that they should be in confused doubt about a new Creation? \nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ وَنَعْلَمُ مَا تُوَسْوِسُ بِهٖ نَفْسُهٗ ۖۚ وَنَحْنُ اَقْرَبُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ حَبْلِ الْوَرِيْدِ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA WA NA’LAMO MAA TOOSWESU BEHI NAFSUH WA NAHNO AQRABO ELAYHE MIN HABLE AL-WAREEDE.\nIt was We Who created man, and We know what dark suggestions his soul makes to him: for We are nearer to him than (his) jugular vein. \nاِذْ يَتَلَقَّى الْمُتَلَقِّيٰنِ عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَعَنِ الشِّمَالِ قَعِيْدٌ‏(17)\nIZ YATALAQQAA AL-MUTALAQQEENE A’NIL YAMEENE WA A’NIL SHEMAALE QAE’EEDUN.\nBehold, two (guardian angels) appointed to learn (his doings) learn (and noted them), one sitting on the right and one on the left. \nمَا يَلْفِظُ مِنْ قَوْلٍ اِلَّا لَدَيْهِ رَقِيْبٌ عَتِيْدٌ‏(18)\nMAA YALFEZU MIN QAWLIN ILLAA LADAYHE RAQEEBUN A’ATEEDUN.\nNot a word does he utter but there is a sentinel by him, ready (to note it). \nوَ جَآءَتْ سَكْرَةُ الْمَوْتِ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ مَا كُنْتَ مِنْهُ تَحِيْدُ‏(19)\nWA JAAA-AT SAKRATU MAWT BIL-HAQ ZAALEKA MAA KUNTA MINHO TAHEEDU.\nAnd the stupor of death will bring Truth (before his eyes): “This was the thing which thou wast trying to escape!” \nوَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ الْوَعِيْدِ‏(20)\nWA FIL SOORE ZAA LEKA YAWMUD AL-WAE’EEDE.\nAnd the Trumpet shall be blown: that will be the Day whereof Warning (had been given). \nوَجَآءَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّعَهَا سَآئِقٌ وَّشَهِيْدٌ‏(21)\nWA JAAA-AT KULLO NAFSIM MMAA’AHAA SAAEQUN WWASHAHEEDUN.\nAnd there will come forth every soul: with each will be an (angel) to drive, and an (angel) to bear witness. \nلَقَدْ كُنْتَ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا فَكَشَفْنَا عَنْكَ غِطَآءَكَ فَبَصَرُكَ الْيَوْمَ حَدِيْدٌ‏(22)\nLAQAD KUNTA FEE GHAFLATIM MIN HAAZAA FAKASHAFNAA A’NKAL GHETAAAKA FABASARUKA YAWMA HADEEDUN.\n(It will be said:) “Thou wast heedless of this; now have We removed thy veil, and sharp is thy sight this Day!” \nوَقَالَ قَرِيْنُهٗ هٰذَا مَا لَدَىَّ عَتِيْدٌ ؕ‏(23)\nWA QAALA QAREENUH HAAZAA MAA LADAYYAL A’ATEEDUN.\nAnd his Companion will say: “Here is (his Record) ready with me!” \nاَلْقِيَا فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍۙ‏(24)\nAALQEEA FEE JAHANNAMA KULLA KAFFAARIN A’ANEEDIN.\n(The sentence will be:) “Throw, throw into Hell every contumacious Rejecter (of Allah)!- \nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ مُّرِيْبِ ۙ‏(25)\nMMANNAAA’IN LLELKHAYRE MO’TADIN MMUREEBE.\n“Who forbade what was good, transgressed all bounds, cast doubts and suspicions; \nاۨلَّذِىْ جَعَلَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَاَ لْقِيٰهُ فِى الْعَذَابِ الشَّدِيْدِ‏(26)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FAALQEEHU FIL A’ZAABE ASH-SHADEEDE.\n“Who set up another god beside Allah: Throw him into a severe penalty.” \nقَالَ قَرِيْنُهٗ رَبَّنَا مَاۤ اَطْغَيْتُهٗ وَلٰكِنْ كَانَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(27)\nQAALA QAREENUH RABBANAA MAA AATGHAYTUH WA LAAKIL KAANA FEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nHis Companion will say: “Our Lord! I did not make him transgress, but he was (himself) far astray.” \nقَالَ لَا تَخْتَصِمُوْا لَدَىَّ وَقَدْ قَدَّمْتُ اِلَيْكُمْ بِالْوَعِيْدِ‏(28)\nQAALA LAA TAKHTASEMOOA LADAYYAL WA QAD QADDAMTO ELAYKUM BIL-WAE’EEDE.\nHe will say: “Dispute not with each other in My Presence: I had already in advance sent you Warning. \nمَا يُبَدَّلُ الْقَوْلُ لَدَىَّ وَمَاۤ اَنَا بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِ‏(29)\nMAA YUBADDALU QAWLO LADAYYAL WA MAA ANAA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\n“The Word changes not before Me, and I do not the least injustice to My Servants.” \nيَوْمَ نَقُوْلُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلِ امْتَلَئْتِ وَتَقُوْلُ هَلْ مِنْ مَّزِيْدٍ‏(30)\nYAWMA NAQOOLU LE-JAHANNAMA HALE AMTALATE WA TAQOOLO HAL MIM MMAZEEDIN.\nOne Day We will ask Hell, “Art thou filled to the full?” It will say, “Are there any more (to come)?” \nوَاُزْلِفَتِ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ غَيْرَ بَعِيْدٍ‏(31)\nWAAZLEFATE JANNATO LILMUTTAQEEN GHAYRA BA-E’ED.\nAnd the Garden will be brought nigh to the Righteous, no more a thing distant. \nهٰذَا مَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لِكُلِّ اَوَّابٍ حَفِيْظٍ‌ۚ‏(32)\nHAAZAA MAA TOO-A’DOON LEKULLIM AAWABIN HAFEEZIN.\n(A voice will say:) “This is what was promised for you, for every one who turned (to Allah) in sincere repentance, who kept (His Law), \nمَنْ خَشِىَ الرَّحْمٰنَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَجَآءَ بِقَلْبٍ مُّنِيْبِۙ‏(33)\nMAN KHASHEAAA BIL-GHAYBE BIL-GHAYBE WA JAAA-A BEQALBIN MMUNEEBE.\n“Who feared (Allah) Most Gracious Unseen, and brought a heart turned in devotion (to Him): \nاۨدْخُلُوْهَا بِسَلٰمٍ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُلُوْدِ‏(34)\nADKHULOOHAA BESALAAMIN ZAALEKA YAWMUD AL-KHULOODE.\n“Enter ye therein in Peace and Security; this is a Day of Eternal Life!” \nلَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ فِيْهَا وَلَدَيْنَا مَزِيْدٌ‏(35)\nLAHUM MAA YASHAAOONA FEEHAA WA LADAYNAA MAZEEDUN.\nThere will be for them therein all that they wish, and more besides in Our Presence. \nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ بَطْشًا فَنَقَّبُوْا فِى الْبِلَادِ ؕ هَلْ مِنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(36)\nWA AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HUM ASHADDO MINHUM BATSHAN FANAQQABOOA FIL BELAADE HAL MIM MAHEES.\nBut how many generations before them did We destroy (for their sins), stronger in power than they? Then did they wander through the land: was there any place of escape (for them)? \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَذِكْرٰى لِمَنْ كَانَ لَهٗ قَلْبٌ اَوْ اَلْقَى السَّمْعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيْدٌ‏(37)\nINNAL FEE ZAALEKA LAZEKRAA LEMAN-Y KAANA LAHU QALBUN AW AALQAA JA-A’LA WA HOWA WA.\nVerily in this is a Message for any that has a heart and understanding or who gives ear and earnestly witnesses (the truth). \nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ‌ۖ وَّمَا مَسَّنَا مِنْ لُّغُوْبٍ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN WA MAA MASSANAA MIN LLUGHOOBIN.\nWe created the heavens and the earth and all between them in Six Days, nor did any sense of weariness touch Us. \nفَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوْعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ الْغُرُوْبِ‌ۚ‏(39)\nFAS-BIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA QABLA TULOOE’E ASH-SHAMSE WA QABLA AL-GHUROOBE.\nBear, then, with patience, all that they say, and celebrate the praises of thy Lord, before the rising of the sun and before (its) setting. \nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاَدْبَارَ السُّجُوْدِ‏(40)\nWA MENAN LAYLE FASABBEHHU WAADBAARA SOJOOD.\nAnd during part of the night, (also,) celebrate His praises, and (so likewise) after the postures of adoration. \nوَاسْتَمِعْ يَوْمَ يُنَادِ الْمُنَادِ مِنْ مَّكَانٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ‏(41)\nWAASTAMEA’ YAWMA YUNAADE AL-MUNAADE MIM MAKAANIM QAREEBIN.\nAnd listen for the Day when the Caller will call out from a place quiet near, \nيَوْمَ يَسْمَعُوْنَ الصَّيْحَةَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُرُوْجِ‏(42)\nYAWMA YAS-MA-O’ONA AS-SAYHATA BIL-HAQQE ZAA LEKA YAWMUD AL-KHUROOJE.\nThe Day when they will hear a (mighty) Blast in (very) truth: that will be the Day of Resurrection. \nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْىٖ وَنُمِيْتُ وَاِلَيْنَا الْمَصِيْرُۙ‏(43)\nINNAA NAHNO NUHAA WANUMEETU WA ELAYNAA MASEER.\nVerily it is We Who give Life and Death; and to Us is the Final Goal- \nيَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ الْاَرْضُ عَنْهُمْ سِرَاعًا‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ حَشْرٌ عَلَيْنَا يَسِيْرٌ‏(44)\nYAWMA TASHAQQAQU ARZO A’NHUM SERAAA’AN ZAA LEKA HASHRUN A’LAYNAA YASEERUN.\nThe Day when the Earth will be rent asunder, from (men) hurrying out: that will be a gathering together, quite easy for Us. \nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ‌ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِجَبَّارٍ‌ فَذَكِّرْ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ مَنْ يَّخَافُ وَعِيْدِ‏(45)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAQOOLOONA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEJABBAARIN FA-ZAKKIR BE-QUR-AANE MAN YYAKHAAFU WAE’EEDE.\nWe know best what they say; and thou art not one to overawe them by force. So admonish with the Qur'an such as fear My Warning! ",
  "merits": "Surah Qaaf\nThis Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 45 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites this Surah frequently will not suffer at the time of death. Reciting Surah Qaaf in salaat increases one’s sustenance and makes the accounting of the Day of Judgement easy.\nWriting and drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures one of many acute diseases. Verse 23 of this Surah is especially good for the cure of eye ailments. One can recite this verse and blow into some water and then drink it, and by the will of Allah (s.w.t.) any problem with eyes will be cured."
}
